[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vcpkg/issues/comments/576727330","html_url":"https://github.com/microsoft/vcpkg/issues/9781#issuecomment-576727330","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vcpkg/issues/9781","id":576727330,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDU3NjcyNzMzMA==","user":{"login":"katusk","id":875677,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3NTY3Nw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/875677?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/katusk","html_url":"https://github.com/katusk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/katusk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/katusk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/katusk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/katusk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/katusk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/katusk/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/katusk/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/katusk/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/katusk/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2020-01-21T15:14:14Z","updated_at":"2020-01-21T15:20:35Z","body":"Hmm, both\r\n\r\n- https://github.com/microsoft/vcpkg/blob/master/toolsrc/src/vcpkg/export.cpp#L456 and\r\n- https://github.com/microsoft/vcpkg/blob/master/toolsrc/src/vcpkg/commands.exportifw.cpp#L477\r\n\r\ncall `Install::install_files_and_write_listfile` (searched for \"Exporting package\"), that does what its name suggests, and checks for the source directory (searched for \"Source directory\"; this is substituted for the appropriate subdirectory under `packages` if I am not mistaken) at\r\n\r\n- https://github.com/microsoft/vcpkg/blob/master/toolsrc/src/vcpkg/install.cpp#L55\r\n\r\nI think we should call something like `read_listfile_and_export_files` (just made this name up) at this point and skip checks that are related to the `packages` directory.\r\n\r\nIn my mind, at least, the natural sequence of steps for a `vcpkg install` (points 1-4) and then a `vcpkg export` (point 5) are the following:\r\n\r\n1. Download the package (`downloads` directory)\r\n2. Build the package (`buildtrees` directory)\r\n3. Gather build artifacts for install (`packages` directory)\r\n4. Install the package (`installed` directory)\r\n5. Export the package (custom export directory)\r\n\r\n...where every step should only rely on files from a previous step, I think. And I also consider the directories in points 1-3 to be temporary that could be deleted at any time based on the behaviour and help description of the `--clean-after-build` switch.\r\n\r\nPlease let me know what is the best way to proceed, and I am happy to send a PR with the necessary changes.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vcpkg/issues/comments/576727330/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"katusk","id":875677,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg3NTY3Nw==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/875677?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/katusk","html_url":"https://github.com/katusk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/katusk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/katusk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/katusk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/katusk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/katusk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/katusk/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/katusk/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/katusk/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/katusk/received_events","type":"User